From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 00:36:57 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] dom0-xt: take the Xen public headers from zephyr-xenlib


Zephyr used to vendor its own trimmed copy of the Xen public headers under
include/zephyr/xen/public/. Upstream removed it (commit d58fbb8cfc58,
backported here as 0024) and made zephyr-xenlib the single source: xenlib's
include/xen/public/ is a byte-for-byte copy of Xen 4.21.0's public headers,
and its CMakeLists.txt puts that directory on the include path
unconditionally.

This matters beyond the missing file. The two header trees used identical
include guards (__XEN_PUBLIC_DOMCTL_H__ and friends) while defining
*different* layouts, so whichever tree a translation unit reached first won
and the other became a silent no-op. sizeof(struct xen_arch_domainconfig) was
12 in the Zephyr copy and 16 in xenlib's (the latter has the trailing
`arm_sci_type` that Xen 4.21 actually expects), which is a one-definition-rule
violation the linker cannot see: xstat.c got 16 bytes while xen-dom-mgmt.c got
12. With the vendored copy gone there is exactly one definition, and it is the
one Xen agrees with.

src/dom_cfg/rpi_4b.c is included here rather than fixed in 0020, which adds it:
0020 is the RPi4 board's guest configuration and stays as close to what it was as
possible, while this patch's whole job is the header move for zephyr-dom0-xt. The
consequence is an ordering constraint - 0019/0020 must be applied before this one,
which is why apply-zephyr-patches.sh no longer keeps them at the end of the series.

Depends on 0024 (zephyr), and on 0020 for src/dom_cfg/rpi_4b.c.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5[1m]
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending [xen-troops/zephyr-dom0-xt]
---
diff --git a/src/dom_cfg/rpi_4b.c b/src/dom_cfg/rpi_4b.c
--- a/src/dom_cfg/rpi_4b.c
+++ b/src/dom_cfg/rpi_4b.c
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <domain.h>
-#include <zephyr/xen/public/domctl.h>
+#include <xen/public/domctl.h>
 #include <string.h>
 #include <xl_parser.h>
 #include "../dom0.h"
